    {
      "short": "Replicate",
      "chapter": "technique",
      "title": "Replication — redundancy as a way of life",
      "body": [
        "<span class=\"term\">Replication</span> keeps live copies on independent machines — one fails, another serves. Replicas also add read capacity for free(ish).",
        "But the write stream still flows through one primary, and copies arrive <em>asynchronously</em> — replicas lag behind under write load."
      ],
      "callout": {
        "kind": "insight",
        "text": "Async replication = eventual consistency on replicas: a user can write, then read a replica that hasn't caught up, and see their data 'missing'."
      },
